\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Rate-distortion frontier of 3DGS compression.} TurboSplat{} (blue curve) traces the Pareto frontier of training-free compression with provable optimality guarantees. Competing methods (individual markers) achieve higher ratios but require GPU access and/or training. The dotted vertical line marks the approximate quantization wall (${\sim }10{\times }$) beyond which training-free methods require Gaussian merging. The dashed horizontal line indicates zero quality loss.\relax }}{9}{figure.caption.26}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rd_frontier}{{1}{9}{\textbf {Rate-distortion frontier of 3DGS compression.} \ours {} (blue curve) traces the Pareto frontier of training-free compression with provable optimality guarantees. Competing methods (individual markers) achieve higher ratios but require GPU access and/or training. The dotted vertical line marks the approximate quantization wall (${\sim }10{\times }$) beyond which training-free methods require Gaussian merging. The dashed horizontal line indicates zero quality loss.\relax }{figure.caption.26}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {SH overfitting analysis.} (a)\nonbreakingspace Overfitting gap $G$ versus compression-induced PSNR change for all 21 scenes. High-gap scenes (drjohnson, playroom, treehill) cluster near zero compression loss, confirming the ``damage budget'' hypothesis. Scenes with genuine view-dependent content (mic, ficus) suffer more despite moderate gaps. (b)\nonbreakingspace Average overfitting ratio $R_{k}$ per SH band on NeRF Synthetic, showing the consistent hierarchy $R_{1} < R_{2} < R_{3}$. The dashed line at $R_{k}{=}1$ indicates zero overfitting; $R_{3}{=}2.45$ implies ${\sim }59\%$ of band\nonbreakingspace 3 content is noise.\relax }}{9}{figure.caption.27}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:overfitting}{{2}{9}{\textbf {SH overfitting analysis.} (a)~Overfitting gap $G$ versus compression-induced PSNR change for all 21 scenes. High-gap scenes (drjohnson, playroom, treehill) cluster near zero compression loss, confirming the ``damage budget'' hypothesis. Scenes with genuine view-dependent content (mic, ficus) suffer more despite moderate gaps. (b)~Average overfitting ratio $\R {k}$ per SH band on NeRF Synthetic, showing the consistent hierarchy $\R {1} < \R {2} < \R {3}$. The dashed line at $\R {k}{=}1$ indicates zero overfitting; $\R {3}{=}2.45$ implies ${\sim }59\%$ of band~3 content is noise.\relax }{figure.caption.27}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Quantization wall and per-scene results.} (a)\nonbreakingspace Position bit sensitivity on \textit  {stump}: each bit removed below 16 incurs ${\sim }0.86\,\text  {dB}$ additional loss, establishing 16-bit positions as the minimum for COLMAP scenes. This sensitivity defines the quantization wall---the fundamental limit of training-free compression. (b)\nonbreakingspace Per-scene PSNR change at the balanced operating point ($9.1{\times }$ average), sorted by increasing loss. Four scenes (playroom, drjohnson, treehill, garden) achieve effectively free compression; playroom \emph  {improves} under compression.\relax }}{10}{figure.caption.28}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:wall}{{3}{10}{\textbf {Quantization wall and per-scene results.} (a)~Position bit sensitivity on \textit {stump}: each bit removed below 16 incurs ${\sim }0.86\dB $ additional loss, establishing 16-bit positions as the minimum for COLMAP scenes. This sensitivity defines the quantization wall---the fundamental limit of training-free compression. (b)~Per-scene PSNR change at the balanced operating point ($9.1{\times }$ average), sorted by increasing loss. Four scenes (playroom, drjohnson, treehill, garden) achieve effectively free compression; playroom \emph {improves} under compression.\relax }{figure.caption.28}{}}
